-- 6956 -- Finhead Paladin Adventurer
#newmonster 6956
#copystats 1783
#spr1 "ForgottenRealms/dragonbait.tga"
#spr2 "ForgottenRealms/dragonbait2.tga"
#name "Finhead Paladin Adventurer"
#nametype 113 -- Male C'Tis
#descr "The most famous Finhead Paladin was Dragonbait. He was the legendary soul-brother of the adventurer, Alias. Transported to Faerun alongside a small community of his people by the Rotting God Moander, they formed a small community in the Lost Vale near Shadowdale in the Dalelands.

He worshipped his peoples' god of justice, and received his blessings while in Faerun from Tyr. His divine sense became the rare ability to read thoughts, feelings, desires, and goals of those around him. This only added to his already exceptional skills in combat not only with a variety of weapons he had mastered but also in the close-combat traditions of his people and incorporated his claws and tail into a unique and effective fighting style. Like all saurials, he was extremely vulnerable to the cold. 

He never learned to speak Common despite great effort and instead communicated in a complex series of clicks, chirps, whistles, bodylanguage and scents, which ranged from honeysuckle, to ham, to brimstone. His closest friend and soul-sister, Alias, eventually taught him thieves' cant. 

The nature of his bond with Alias came from her creation - she was a construct, and it was a shard of Dragonbait's soul that was used to give her life. Dragonbait should have died in the ritual, but Alias awoke before the spell was completed and seeing Dragonbait lying beside her and near death, she cradled the saurial and began singing the ancestral Soul Songs of his people. The caster of the ritual, Finder Wyvernspur - a great-bard-turned-demigod - realized the purity in her soul and instead of completing the ritual, helped the two escape from Westgate to Cormyr and eventually back to the Dalelands."
